{"reference":"1 Chronicles 3","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Genealogy","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter traces David’s family and the royal line that follows through Solomon. Within the larger sequence of genealogies and registers in 1 Chronicles 1–9, it is part of a selective presentation linking the restored community with Adam, Israel’s tribes, David, priests, Levites, and preexilic Jerusalem.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 3:1-24"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_003_b87f9668bb0e89c354809115"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Larger Genealogical Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The genealogies surrounding this chapter are best read as selective literary maps of kinship, land, office, and restored identity, rather than as exhaustive modern-style biological pedigrees. Gaps, parallel lines, differing names, and compressed generations therefore need to be considered case by case.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 1:1-54","1 Chronicles 2:1-55","1 Chronicles 4:1-43","1 Chronicles 5:1-26","1 Chronicles 6:1-81","1 Chronicles 7:1-40","1 Chronicles 8:1-40","1 Chronicles 9:1-44"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_003_45fe3d11e445a4c89ee3c44f"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}